WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.770
- [Instructor] We're told
this table defines function f.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.780
All right.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.680
For every x, they give us
the corresponding f of x.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.460
According to the table, is
f even, odd, or neither?

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.650
So pause this video and see

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.090
if you can figure that out on your own.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:18.960
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.930
So let's just remind
ourselves the definition

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.690
of even and odd.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.490
One definition that we can
think of is that f of x,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.620
if f of x is equal to f of negative x,

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.410
then we're dealing with an even function.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.460
And if f of x is equal

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.690
to the negative of f of negative x,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.210
or another way of saying
that, if f of negative x.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.830
If f of negative x, instead
of it being equal to f of x,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.870
it's equal to negative f of x.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.850
These last two are equivalent.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.170
Then in these situations,

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.840
we are dealing with an odd function.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.130
And if neither of these are true,

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.010
then we're dealing with neither.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.290
So what about what's going on over here?

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.800
So let's see.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.680
F of negative seven is
equal to negative one.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.470
What about f of the
negative of negative seven?

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.290
Well, that would be f of seven.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:14.030
And we see f of seven here is
also equal to negative one.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.280
So at least in that case and that case,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.670
if we think of x as seven,

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:24.590
f of x is equal to f of negative x.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:25.890
So it works for that.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.750
It also works for
negative three and three.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.330
F of three is equal to
f of negative three.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.030
They're both equal to two.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.900
And you can see and you can
kind of visualize in your head

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.500
that we have symmetry around the y-axis.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.960
And so this looks like an even function.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.010
So I will circle that in.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.260
Let's do another example.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.020
So here, once again, the
table defines function f.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.560
It's a different function f.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.840
Is this function even, odd, or neither?

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.490
So pause this video and
try to think about it.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.980
All right, so let's
just try a few examples.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.820
So here we have f of five is equal to two.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.100
F of five is equal to two.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.650
What is f of negative five?

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.820
F of negative five.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.610
Not only is it not equal to two,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.920
it would have to be equal to two

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.540
if this was an even function.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.800
And it would be equal to negative two

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.860
if this was an odd
function, but it's neither.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.950
So we very clearly see just
looking at that data point

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.250
that this can neither be even, nor odd.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:30.040
So I would say neither or
neither right over here.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.340
Let's do one more example.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.540
Once again, the table defines function f.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.690
According to the table, is
it even, odd, or neither?

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.630
Pause the video again.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.533
Try to answer it.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.860
All right, so actually
let's just start over here.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.070
So we have f of four is
equal to negative eight.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.760
What is f of negative four?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.200
And the whole idea here is I wanna say,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.050
okay, if f of x is equal to something,

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.770
what is f of negative x?

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.920
Well, they luckily give
us f of negative four.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.330
It is equal to eight.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.810
So it looks like it's not equal to f of x.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.730
It's equal to the negative of f of x.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.010
This is equal to the
negative of f of four.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:09.980
So on that data point alone,

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.020
at least that data point
satisfies it being odd.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.490
It's equal to the negative of f of x.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.400
But now let's try the other
points just to make sure.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.020
So f of one is equal to five.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.033
What is f of negative one?

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.350
Well, it is equal to negative five.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.780
Once again, f of negative x is equal

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.240
to the negative of f of x.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.370
So that checks out.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.940
And then f of zero,

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.870
well, f of zero is of
course equal to zero.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.840
But of course if you say

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.930
what is the negative of f of,

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.940
if you say what f of negative of zero,

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.520
well, that's still f of zero.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.190
And then if you were to
take the negative of zero,

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.730
that's still zero.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.160
So you could view this.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.610
This is consistent still with being odd.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:00.990
This you could view as the
negative of f of negative zero,

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.120
which of course is still going to be zero.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.023
So this one is looking
pretty good that it is odd.

